WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.510
A student's department assistant was asked

2
00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:06.030
to remind one student about a deadline.

3
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:10.160
It emailed all three thousand students,

4
00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:12.240
using the department's account.

5
00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:14.750
No one had to approve it.

6
00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:16.280
Who is responsible?

7
00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.860
Today: why agents that act need limits,

8
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.800
how permissions and human approval keep

9
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:26.840
them safe, and how to teach students to

10
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:29.020
design accountable agent systems.

11
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:34.560
Once an agent can send, buy or delete, its

12
00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:36.660
mistakes become actions in the world.

13
00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:38.440
Some actions are

14
00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:40.540
reversible and some are not.

15
00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.700
Safety design starts by sorting them.

16
00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:46.770
Give the agent only the tools

17
00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:48.490
and scopes its task needs.

18
00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:51.940
A reminder agent needs to email one

19
00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:53.760
student, not the whole list.

20
00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:56.890
Narrow, per-task permissions turn a

21
00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.370
disaster into a refused request.

22
00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:02.430
Route irreversible or

23
00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:04.950
wide-reaching actions through a human.

24
00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:07.950
The agent drafts the message and

25
00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:09.210
shows who will receive it.

26
00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:11.840
A person approves or rejects it,

27
00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:13.360
and the decision is logged.

28
00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:17.190
Frameworks such as the NIST AI Risk

29
00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:19.790
Management Framework ask teams to map,

30
00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:23.030
measure, manage and govern risks.

31
00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:26.520
For agents this means naming who is

32
00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:29.700
accountable, logging every action, and

33
00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.500
planning how to stop the system.

34
00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:34.570
Students tend to add safety

35
00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:36.350
at the end, if at all.

36
00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:39.140
Make every agent project begin

37
00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:40.760
with a short risk review.

38
00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.980
List each tool, its worst misuse,

39
00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:46.360
whether it is reversible, and what

40
00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:47.920
limit or approval applies.

41
00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:49.690
Quick check!

42
00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:52.120
The assistant can read the

43
00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:54.620
timetable, draft a message, and

44
00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:55.980
send it to a mailing list.

45
00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:58.800
Which action should need human approval?

46
00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:01.260
Sending to the list.

47
00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:03.750
Reading and drafting change

48
00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:05.090
nothing in the world.

49
00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:07.850
Sending is irreversible and

50
00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:09.450
reaches thousands of people.

51
00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:13.010
In the app, open the approvals lab.

52
00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:16.010
Decide which of the agent's actions to

53
00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:19.730
allow, limit or send for approval, and

54
00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:21.330
see what happens to each request.

55
00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:23.160
Your turn.

56
00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:26.030
Which design would have prevented the

57
00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:28.310
email to all three thousand students?

58
00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:32.290
A per-task recipient limit plus

59
00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:34.550
human approval for any bulk send.

60
00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:38.270
Remember: sort actions by reversibility,

61
00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:41.750
give least privilege, route risky actions

62
00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:44.810
to a person, and log everything.

63
00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:48.830
Try it in your next lecture: give groups

64
00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:51.250
the tool list of a campus assistant agent.

65
00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:54.980
Each group fills a table of worst misuse,

66
00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:58.560
reversibility and control for every tool.

67
00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:00.970
Then compare tables and agree

68
00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:02.170
on the approval rules.
